{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the least probable outcomes of each lottery, defined as the outcome with the minimum probability in each respective lottery. For Lottery A, the least probable outcome is 2500 Euros with a probability of 33%. For Lottery B, the least probable outcome is 2400 Euros with a probability of 34%. The reason compares these least probable outcomes and prefers the lottery with the more favorable (i.e., higher monetary value) of these two outcomes. Since 2500 Euros (A) is greater than 2400 Euros (B), the decision reason would prefer Lottery A. Thus, the reason is applicable to the decision problem, and the relevant information (the least probable outcomes and their values) can be clearly derived from the lotteries’ structures.",
